Z||000009||avengador1||11-11-2001||11:08 PM||||In Connecticut anything that fires a projectile is considered a firearm(tough gun laws). I don't know what the law is were you live, but here, that is what they charge people with that use paint guns in public. We do have legitimate places to use these for capture the flag, war games, etc. My point is two wrongs don't make a right. I have been down that path before and all that will happen is that your problem with these punks will escalate. Try calling their parents, or better yet have your parents call their parents, and let them know that you want them to pay for any damages you have incured because of their children, treaten to sue. Believe me when I tell you that when you get the parents involved, and they know they can be sued, they will talk to their children and fix their asses. A paintball is not a toy and can rob you of your sight or hearing if it hits you just right, it can even kill you under the right circumstances. Im not against paintball guns, I think they are fun if used the right way. I know Im beginning to sound like an old fart, Im 42 and have a 10 year old son. If I ever found out he was doing stuff like these kids, I would ream him a new hole. It is not worth it for one to be sued for his own kids stupidness. I know this sounds like a wimp out, and the kids will try to get back at you. Just make sure that their parents know you will hold them personally responsible for any and all damages, and to keep their dammed kids away from you or your family, or you will get the police involved next. You should also stay away from them. They probably are cowards who travel in a pack to make themselves feel superior. I bet if you catch any of them by themselves they will piss their pants. These kids sound like bullies and don't deserve any respect or code of silence. Just my 2 cents worth speaking from personal experience.||||reg||1
