Z||000020||fieroX||11-12-2001||04:21 AM||||find a place in your town that sells plastics, like epoxies and such, but thats their only business, not like a hardware store.  Get one gallon of liquid expanding foam.  This stuff is awesome.  Its sort of like the stuff in the can, but stays liquid for about a minute before expanding.  <BR>Now this is going to cost you about 50 bucks but will cost them way more.  Get a gallon of this stuff, a small hand pump and a plastic tube about 15 feet long about 1/2 inch in inside diameter.  Hook the pump to the tube.  Now late one night real late like 3am take this equipment to this guys house go to the rear of his car and shove the plastic tube as far as you can up his exhaust pipe.  Hopefully he has a straight through muffler or it will stop there.  If you can get the tube through the muffler ram it as far up the exhaust system as you can, and start pumping.  This stuff expands 20 fold.  It will creep up all the way through the cat, if he has one, and through the exhaust manifolds, into the heads, hopefully a few exhaust valves are cracked open, and into the cylinders.  Needless to say when this guy trys to start his car, he is going to crap his pants.  Just hope he has straight through mufflers, glass packs are good for this, if he doesnt have a cat, this should work even better.  When the foam stops spreading and hardening things will start cracking.  It will be cool.<p>[This message has been edited by fieroX (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||1
